woman|adult-female-person|NOUN|Adult female person|An adult female human being.|người phụ nữ|The woman at the information desk helped us find the exhibition.|Người phụ nữ ở quầy thông tin giúp chúng tôi tìm khu triển lãm.|Countable; singular woman, plural women. Use women doctors rather than woman doctors.|0
class|group-of-students|NOUN|Group of students|A group of students who are taught together.|lớp học; nhóm học sinh|Our class made a mural for the library wall.|Lớp chúng tôi làm một bức tranh tường cho thư viện.|Countable; a class of students. Collective agreement varies by variety and emphasis.|0
class|teaching-session|NOUN|Teaching session|A period during which a teacher teaches a subject or skill.|buổi học; giờ học|The pottery class starts after lunch on Saturdays.|Buổi học làm gốm bắt đầu sau bữa trưa vào các ngày thứ Bảy.|Countable; attend a class, a class in a subject. Distinguish one session from the group attending it.|1
class|social-category|NOUN|Social category|A group in society whose members have a similar economic or social position.|tầng lớp xã hội|The historian compared housing conditions across different social classes.|Nhà sử học so sánh điều kiện nhà ở giữa các tầng lớp xã hội khác nhau.|Countable; social class, the middle class. Class does not establish an individual's abilities or worth.|2
fond|feeling-affection-or-liking|ADJECTIVE|Feeling affection or liking|Having affection for someone or enjoying something.|yêu mến; thích|My uncle is fond of growing tomatoes on his balcony.|Chú tôi thích trồng cà chua trên ban công.|Fond of plus noun or -ing; fonder, fondest. Fond is not ordinarily used as a verb.|0
irritate|make-annoyed|VERB|Make annoyed|To cause someone to feel annoyed, often through repeated actions.|làm khó chịu; chọc tức|The repeated clicking irritated the people reading nearby.|Tiếng lách cách liên tục khiến những người đang đọc gần đó khó chịu.|Transitive; irritate someone. Irritating describes the cause; irritated describes the person.|-
irritate|cause-physical-discomfort|VERB|Cause physical discomfort|To make a part of the body sore, itchy or uncomfortable.|gây kích ứng|The rough collar irritated the skin on his neck.|Cổ áo thô ráp gây kích ứng vùng da ở cổ anh ấy.|Transitive; irritate skin or eyes. Irritation is a noun; this example describes discomfort rather than treatment.|-
not|grammatical-negation|ADVERB|Grammatical negation|Used to make a statement or part of a statement negative.|không; không phải|The parcel is not heavy, but it is too wide for this shelf.|Bưu kiện không nặng, nhưng quá rộng đối với chiếc kệ này.|Usually follows an auxiliary or be; use do not with most simple present verbs. Often contracts to n't.|0,1
